(TIM-47 - starting a timer that has already run restarts it: the second
 duration measures only the second job, not both. Undocumented; the manual
 says nothing about a second Start.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox TIM-47.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   the first run measured its 1200 milliseconds
   the restart reset the clock rather than accumulating
)
a timer called lap.
Start the lap.
Wait 1200 milliseconds.
Stop the lap.
a number called 'the first run' is lap's duration in milliseconds.
Start the lap.
Wait 300 milliseconds.
Stop the lap.
a number called 'the second run' is lap's duration in milliseconds.
If 'the first run' is greater than 1199 then, print "the first run measured its 1200 milliseconds".
Otherwise, print "the first run measured {'the first run'} milliseconds".
If 'the second run' is less than 'the first run' then, print "the restart reset the clock rather than accumulating".
Otherwise, print "the second run measured {'the second run'} milliseconds, so the timer accumulated".
